Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:03.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}How is the wind learned?\NWith a simple trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.07,0:00:09.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Keep one coordinate of each point, and\Nlay the transport clock out to the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.47,0:00:12.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Pair each noise point\Nwith a random snapshot;
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.43,0:00:14.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}join them with a straight string.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.18,0:00:18.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Thousands of strings, crossing everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.96,0:00:21.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Pick one place, at one moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.22,0:00:25.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Several strings pass through,\Npointing different ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.13,0:00:30.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The network learns one arrow\Nthere: their {\c&HF09CB4&}average direction{\c&HF7F4F2&}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.82,0:00:33.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}That is the whole training:\Nplain regression,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.77,0:00:36.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}like fitting a curve through points.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.20,0:00:40.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Follow the averaged wind, not the strings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.59,0:00:44.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The paths bend, and drawn against\Nthe clock, they never cross.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.32,0:00:50.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Learn the average exactly, and the\Nnoise lands exactly on the data's crowd.
